  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 25 June 2026, the proposal as shown on the drawing(s) submitted on 12/05/2026 and numbered 23120-PP-001, 23120_PP_309, 23120_PP_308, 23120_PP_307, 23120_PP_306, 23120_PP_302, 23120_PP_301, 23120_PP_201, 23120_PP_300, 23120_PP_200, 23120_PP_104, 23120_PP_100, 23120_PP_101, 23120_PP_105, 23120_PP_106, 23120_PP_107, was lawful within the meanings of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 because:\r\n\r\nThe proposed works described in the application would not constitute \"development\" for the purposes of Section 55 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended), as they would not involve a material change in the use of land and/or operational development. As such, the proposal would be considered lawful under section 191 or 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act (as amended).\r\n"
